  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the driver in the scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the driver (the person being questioned by the sheriff) through the use of the second-line text 'because you scored low on the asvab?'. The word 'you' directly addresses the driver, creating a deictic reference that positions the viewer as the person being questioned, thereby projecting the user's identity onto the driver's role in the scene. This projection is reinforced by the driver's gesture of defense, which invites the user to imagine themselves in that position.",
